<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέρτρον</span></b> , τό<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽδέρὠ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίπλους</span>
			, <i>caul</i> or <i>membrane which conlains the bowels,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολάδας δέρτροισι καλύψεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					45
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				5.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῦπε . . δέρτρον ἔσω
			δύνοντες</span> even to <i>the bowels,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.579
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l.c., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέρτρον</span> is expld. by
			Gramm., as <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				257.31
			</span></i>, etc., of the vulture's <i>beak</i>: hence, of <i>a sharp
				point,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				880
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύμπανα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
